{
  "description": "T3\tGleditsia\tThis tree has several over extended lateral limbs growing towards the Magnolia group along with a small Ganoderma fungal bracket at the base of the trunk. \rReduce lower lateral limbs by 2.5-3m in length.\rReduce remainder of the crown by 1.5-2m all round and shape.\rRemove deadwood throughout.\rReasons for work - To mitigate the risk of limb failure.\rT8\tCotoneaster\tReduce by 1.5m and shape. Raise lower canopy to 2.2m above ground level.\rT11\tWhitebeam\tTree has a large fungal bracket at the base.\rThis coupled with the fact that the tree is heavily leaning towards the buildings could result in stem failure and damage to the buildings.\rFell to ground level.",
